From: pocket-debs <masterxq@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] modem-daemon: connect to each modem once
Description:
 The controller connected to the signals of every modem again whenever a
 modem was added or removed, without removing the earlier connections, and
 the connections kept the modem objects alive (QSharedPointer captures)
 after ModemManagerQt had dropped them. After ModemManager restarted, the
 old objects listened on the same object paths as the new ones: one call
 was announced and deleted as often as modems had appeared before (ten
 times after a few restarts), and its SIM was taken from an outdated
 object.
 .
 Each modem object now gets one receiver object for all its connections;
 it is deleted when the modem is removed or replaced by a new object under
 the same path, which disconnects and releases the interfaces. The
 lambdas capture the modem path instead of the modem object. A modem that
 ModemManagerQt announces again because it got more interfaces keeps its
 calls. A removed modem takes its calls with it (callDeleted), and finished
 call objects are freed.
Forwarded: no
License: LicenseRef-KDE-Accepted-GPL (as the patched files)
Last-Update: 2026-11-25
